Z||000000||BlackFiero86SE||06-24-2001||01:24 PM||||I am new to the forum and I have two or three problems with my 86 SE V6 w/114000 miles.  The first is that I just had the brakes replaced and now when I turn the wheels squeak.  The squeaks pitch varies with the rotational speed of the wheels and goes away when the wheels are straight and also when I press the brakes.  (Both are not required at the same time to make the squeak stop.)  The second problem is that sometimes (only when cold) the engine starts and then suddenly dies if I don't floor it.  The third problem is that when it warms up, the tach will start to jump and it will occasionally misfire at highway speeds (65-75).  I unplugged the tach filter, but the problem still remains.  I need some help relatively quickly because I am 17 and this is my daily driver to work.  One other note:  I am only getting 20 mpg max out of the engine even if I baby it.||||reg||4
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||06-24-2001||03:27 PM||||I would check your front wheel bearings  although I dont think that they would skweak or squeel If they were going bad,it probaly would be more of a griding noise.and I would also check to make sure brake pads and the calipers are Installed proerly .I f you had this done by a repair shop Take it back to them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RacinRob||06-24-2001||11:09 PM||||You might have got grease or something on them when the brakes were changed.  It might be dying in the morning because the cold start injector is going bad. and 20 MPG max is not too far off.  I would get some repair manuals if I were you.||||reg||1
